00:00:50.591 --> 00:00:53.761
- [Voiceover] Mike asks,
"Shark Tank's Barbara Corcoran

00:00:53.761 --> 00:00:55.839
doesn't invest in rich kids' businesses.

00:00:55.839 --> 00:00:58.880
How do you feel about
entrepreneurs from privilege?"

00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:01.458
- You know, Babs from the Shark Tank is

00:01:01.458 --> 00:01:04.720
one of my favorite characters,
I like calling Barbara Babs,

00:01:04.720 --> 00:01:06.276
that's just something
I've been doing for years.

00:01:06.276 --> 00:01:08.296
Barbara Long, if you're watching,
that's where it started.

00:01:08.296 --> 00:01:10.316
Wine industry chatter.

00:01:10.316 --> 00:01:13.833
You know, look, I was very much, we all

00:01:13.833 --> 00:01:15.179
have our prejudices.

00:01:15.179 --> 00:01:17.235
Since I came from a zero place, I have

00:01:17.235 --> 00:01:20.033
for a long time talked
about the rich kid syndrome.

00:01:20.033 --> 00:01:22.134
Right now I talk about
the Ivy League, if I go

00:01:22.134 --> 00:01:24.154
to an Ivy League school,
I should be a founder

00:01:24.154 --> 00:01:26.080
because Zucks wears a
hoodie, I'm wearing a hoodie

00:01:26.080 --> 00:01:27.729
so this is perfect timing.

00:01:27.729 --> 00:01:31.316
For a long time, I really
pushed against that

00:01:31.316 --> 00:01:32.872
and said they're not
hungry enough, they're not

00:01:32.872 --> 00:01:33.836
pushed enough.

00:01:33.836 --> 00:01:35.832
My kids are going to be
rich kids, and I think

00:01:35.832 --> 00:01:37.399
what I've learned as I've gotten older,

00:01:37.399 --> 00:01:40.174
39 tomorrow, and because of one or two

00:01:40.174 --> 00:01:42.437
very special friends in my
life right now that grew up

00:01:42.437 --> 00:01:45.329
very wealthy but are hungry and fiery

00:01:45.329 --> 00:01:47.894
and making stuff happen,
I think it comes down to

00:01:47.894 --> 00:01:49.055
anything like a business.

00:01:49.055 --> 00:01:50.611
I talked about VaynerMedia, I
just had an amazing meeting

00:01:50.611 --> 00:01:52.235
with somebody and they're
like, this place is so

00:01:52.235 --> 00:01:53.837
caring and so good.

00:01:53.837 --> 00:01:55.394
I thought it was going
to get worse when we got

00:01:55.394 --> 00:01:57.588
to 400 versus 150, and I said look,

00:01:57.588 --> 00:01:58.876
it stems from the top.

00:01:58.876 --> 00:02:01.511
I actually give a crap, and I
think that trickles through.

00:02:01.511 --> 00:02:03.090
That's the same thing on this.

00:02:03.090 --> 00:02:06.499
I, when I meet rich kids,
and see their pitches,

00:02:06.499 --> 00:02:10.502
spend 45 out of the 50
minutes asking them about

00:02:10.502 --> 00:02:14.467
how they were raised, how
their parents played the game.

00:02:14.467 --> 00:02:17.509
The reason I think my rich
kids are going to be OK

00:02:17.509 --> 00:02:19.993
is because if they act too
rich kiddy, I'm going to

00:02:19.993 --> 00:02:22.036
punch them directly in their mouth.

00:02:22.036 --> 00:02:24.068
What I mean by that is, not like literally

00:02:24.068 --> 00:02:25.507
because I know some of you will freak out.

00:02:25.507 --> 00:02:26.807
Though I may go there, I'm a little weird

00:02:26.807 --> 00:02:27.968
and Eastern European.

00:02:27.968 --> 00:02:30.987
The truth is, I'm going to humble them.

00:02:30.987 --> 00:02:32.728
I'm going to hurt their feelings,

00:02:32.728 --> 00:02:33.866
I'm going to make them cry.

00:02:33.866 --> 00:02:36.404
I'm going to tell them how soft they are.

00:02:36.404 --> 00:02:39.904
I think that it comes
down to the parenting,

00:02:39.904 --> 00:02:43.212
just like it comes down
to the CEO in a business.

00:02:43.212 --> 00:02:45.033
Everything trickles from the top.

00:02:45.033 --> 00:02:47.071
Just because you grew up
with a hundred million dollar

00:02:47.071 --> 00:02:50.291
trust, doesn't mean that
you don't have the hunger

00:02:50.291 --> 00:02:52.463
and just because you grew
up with thirty thousand

00:02:52.463 --> 00:02:54.890
dollars in cash, maybe your
mom did everything for you

00:02:54.890 --> 00:02:56.863
and took care of everything for you.

00:02:56.863 --> 00:02:58.268
It's how you were raised.

00:02:58.268 --> 00:02:59.649
What's the foundation?

00:02:59.649 --> 00:03:01.471
It's the cement.

00:03:01.471 --> 00:03:04.606
My dad, Wine Library was built
to be a 16 floor building

00:03:04.606 --> 00:03:06.266
and everyone made fun of my dad

00:03:06.266 --> 00:03:07.683
from an engineering standpoint.

00:03:07.683 --> 00:03:09.911
He's an old school guy, he
just wants the foundation

00:03:09.911 --> 00:03:12.501
to be strong and there's
too much steel and concrete

00:03:12.501 --> 00:03:14.683
in the basement of Wine Library.

00:03:14.683 --> 00:03:16.528
That's how I think about this question.

00:03:16.528 --> 00:03:17.748
What's the foundation?

00:03:17.748 --> 00:03:20.406
I'm not worried about the
optics, the interior decorating.

00:03:20.406 --> 00:03:22.020
It's the foundation.

